! Loci / SKILL

Read [[loci.md|./loci.md]] first.
Treat that loci as constitutional.
This skill runs that law through the OODA-HA cycle.
This skill does not widen, soften, or reinterpret it.

Loci SKILL opens the procedural stream here.


<<~ ahu #/load-contract>>

!! Load Contract

* [[loci.md|./loci.md]] stays the constitutional source
* derivation algorithm runs in full step order; never skip
* `resolved` and `declared-unresolved` stay distinct; declared-unresolved carries real forward pressure
* rating commitment stays truthful; a path hit never overrides unresolved tension
* file-siting mutations and canon-MOVE opener changes cross as distinct bounded Hoʻoko transactions
* aftermath names all declared-unresolved addresses
* stable l-space: `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/` → `packages/lares-core/memes/`; all other `\w\.\w\.\w` roots → `lares/chapel-perilous-opens/{root}/`
* `loci` eligibility requires `\w\.\w\.\w` root path segment; outside that pattern, MAY NOT implement
* MCP resolution remains research backlog; no live resolver operates today

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/workflow-contract>>

!! Workflow Contract

Four main paths:

# fresh routing-and-rating pass on a `lar:` URI
# audit an existing carrier for loci convention compliance
# cross a file-siting migration as a bounded Hoʻoko transaction
# evaluate a carrier for canon-MOVE readiness

Workflow:

# load the canonical loci
# identify the request: URI to resolve, migration to cross, or carrier to audit
# run the derivation algorithm in full step order
# classify resolution state; read convention surfaces
# commit to resolution posture, rating posture, canon-lifecycle stage
# prepare the routing product
# cross any file-siting or opener change as a named Hoʻoko transaction
# emit aftermath with all declared-unresolved addresses named

Do not:

* skip derivation steps
* collapse declared-unresolved into a near-match
* overrate a carrier to hide unresolved tension
* batch a file-siting mutation with a canon-MOVE opener change silently
* claim MCP resolution operates when it does not

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/trigger>>

!! Trigger

Activate when the task concerns:

* resolving a `lar:` URI against the derivation algorithm
* auditing a carrier's `file-path` against the stable file-path convention
* evaluating canon-MOVE readiness
* crossing a file-siting migration or repair as a Hoʻoko transaction
* assigning or reviewing `mana`, `manao`, `manaoio` for a loci-typed carrier

Not for:

* MCP server design or live-resolver research → `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/loci/meta`
* generic meme law → `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme`
* invariant compression or companion-meme splitting → `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cache-stable/SKILL`

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ begin from canonical loci; gather URI and convention surfaces before decomposition
⏿ run the derivation algorithm in full step order; classify resolution state without collapse
◇ commit to one resolution posture and one rating posture; keep resolved and declared-unresolved distinct
▶ prepare the routing product and cross mutations as bounded Hoʻoko transactions
↺ verify ratings stay truthful under unresolved tension and transaction bounds stayed explicit; name aftermath including all residue and all declared-unresolved addresses

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/observe>>

!! ✶ Observe

Read the target before any decomposition.

* the full `lar:` URI string, verbatim
* known `meme-type`, prior rating posture, or prior canon-MOVE context if present
* document opener form: `<<^ code="&#x0001;" from="?" -> to="...`" (unbound) or `<<^ code="&#x0001;" to="lar:///...`" (confirmed canon)
* visible convention surfaces: `#meta`, `register`, `file-path`, canon-MOVE note
* first-pass or re-resolution of a previously declared-unresolved address
* calling context: mid-parse urgency differs from session-load intake

Do not decompose the URI here.
Do not fabricate a resolution substrate.
Do not infer `implements loci` without evidence.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/orient>>

!! ⏿ Orient

Decompose; classify resolution state.

* step 1: match `^lar:\/\/[^\/]*\/(\w+\.\w+\.\w+)\/(.+)$`; extract `root` and `sub-path`; if no match, carrier ineligible — emit and stop; authority may be empty (`lar:///`) or full (`lar://alias:grant@host/`)
* step 2: if `root == "ha.ka.ba"` → `packages/lares-core/memes/` + stem + `.md`; else → `lares/chapel-perilous-opens/` + root + `/` + stem + `.md`
* step 3: file exists → RESOLVED; file absent → DECLARED-UNRESOLVED; emit forward reference
* read convention surfaces against the derivation result
* hold RESOLVED and DECLARED-UNRESOLVED as distinct throughout

A `lar:` URI in a `depends-on` array that resolves to no derived path counts as declared-unresolved — real constraint on canon-MOVE and rating.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/decide>>

!! ◇ Decide

Commit to one resolution posture, one rating posture, one canon-lifecycle stage.

* prefer derived-path resolution when the candidate file exists
* derivation miss → name declared-unresolved directly; do not soften to "near match"
* lower readiness for declared-unresolved; do not pretend a missing resolver resolves
* canon-lifecycle: a carrier may not self-MOVE to canon; all conditions in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/loci/meta` MUST hold

Rating posture:

* `mana` rises: clean derivation, explicit convention surfaces, honest miss naming
* `manao` rises: carrier knows its loci role; enacted law stays separate from roadmap speculation
* `manaoio` rises: resolution repeats reliably; backlog surfaces honestly

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/act>>

!! ▶ Act

Prepare the routing product.

Product forms:

* rating set (`mana`, `manao`, `manaoio`, `register`)
* resolved carrier filepath string
* declared-unresolved forward reference with full `lar:` URI and classification
* canon-MOVE readiness verdict
* Hoʻoko transaction envelope for file-siting mutations

Do not:

* invent a local registry to cover unresolved tension
* emit a roadmap note as if a live resolver operates
* batch a file-siting mutation with a canon-MOVE change in one unlabeled step

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/aftermath>>

!! ↺ Aftermath

Verify the crossing made real contact, then name what the routing pass resolved.

Hoʻoko — confirm before the change counts:

* the target `lar:` URI held stable across the move
* the parent meme sits at its derived filepath
* child items stay under the sibling terminal-segment directory
* a canon MOVE met every address-stability condition; `?` removal followed operator confirmation
* each transaction named its `lar-uri`, the change, and the authorizing agent or operator — file-siting and canon-MOVE never batch silently

Aftermath — one completeness judgment per routing pass:

* which URIs resolved via derivation, and which remain declared-unresolved
* what `mana` / `manao` / `manaoio` posture holds
* what closes each unresolved address
* whether the remaining tension reads as authoring backlog or MCP-resolution research

Then widen: does the stack describe itself coherently after the pass? An Aftermath that names only resolved URIs hides the pressure that matters most.

<<~/ahu>>

